 "_about": "Block Buffer tables as the Block Buffer editor (BlockBuff.exe, V17, own process, 2026-09-24) SHOWED them - written by hand from screenshots, not by the decoder. Amounts in cm as displayed (the file stores inches x 10000: 0.30 cm = 1181; a percentage of the repeat is stored x 10000 with unit 2: 50% = 500000). ZZBB-USER was an existing scratch table; ZZBB-X1 = ZZBB-USER plus rule 9 (Block, nine distinct amounts) and rule 10 (percentages; the editor demands typed rule numbers); ZZBB-X2 = X1 plus a dynamic percentage and a two-line comment, each saved under a new name. The editor greys out the Segment cells, so segment amounts are 0. Real 3MM (older layout, AccuMark 9) and 3MM-N come from the user's support files with the author comment blanked.",
